-          "quote": "Assume the hypotheses of [[thm-full-memory-bfgs-global-linear-convergence]] and consider an infinite, nonstationary exact-undamped BFGS run with successful strong Wolfe searches. Suppose $G(x)=\\nabla^2 f(x)$ is $L_G$-Lipschitz in operator norm on a neighborhood of $x_*$. With $B_k:=H_k^{-1}$ and $s_k:=x_{k+1}-x_k$, the iterates satisfy\n$$ \\frac{\\|(B_k-G_*)s_k\\|_2}{\\|s_k\\|_2}\\longrightarrow0,\\qquad G_*:=G(x_*). $$\nSince $s_k=\\alpha_kp_k$ with $\\alpha_k>0$, the same limit holds with $p_k$ in place of $s_k$. This is the Dennis–Moré condition used by the local full-memory superlinear convergence result.\n\n",
